31,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems that the projects creating lasting catalogs have aged most gracefully, continuing to be useful long after they ended. Also, the repository is now much faster at processing deposits.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings are concerning. We have a surplus of applicants for coding and modelling, but most trained phenotyping technicians have left for industry. Only the glasshouse crew remains at full strength.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The shared instrumentation is a worry; the spectroscopy suite was idle for eleven weeks due to a lapsed contract. However, the animal facility is now fully accredited with resident vet cover.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears the financial landscape is shifting. While the ministry is kindly subsidizing glasshouse space and computing hours are free, shipping costs are rising and animal-unit rates have become quite steep.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've noticed a worrying pattern in the schedule overruns. Projects relying on live breeding colonies are far more likely to slip, and several field sites have been devastated by flooding and fire recently. Indoor work seems much more stable.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, it is a pity about the technicians, but how wonderful that the glasshouse crew is still with us. Perhaps we can find a project that lets them shine?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, that is a logical conclusion. If the glasshouse crew is the only stable technical resource we have, we should prioritize projects that utilize their specific expertise.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, if the animal-unit rates are steep, we must be cautious. While the animal facility is accredited, the cost might outweigh the benefit for some candidates.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Victoria. It would be a tragedy to award a grant only to have the budget devoured by the vivarium's new pricing before the research even gains momentum.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, I agree. Between the rising costs and the risk of biological delays I found, animal-heavy projects seem quite precarious right now. We should look for something more resilient.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, you make a very sensible point. It would be so stressful for the researchers if their work were interrupted by such unpredictable events. A more stable path seems kinder to everyone.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Benjamin, if computing hours are free and the glasshouse is subsidized, we have a clear path toward projects that are computationally heavy or plant-based. We must avoid anything requiring phenotyping technicians.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, I agree. We must also be wary of any project relying on the spectroscopy suite. If one engineer is covering three institutes, any technical failure could lead to another long period of idleness.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, Victoria. A project that hinges on a single, fragile piece of instrumentation is less a research plan and more a gamble on the reliability of a lapsed contract. Logic suggests we seek stability.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, I'm glad we're on the same page. If we can find a project that balances the free computing and the strong glasshouse support, we can avoid those heartbreaking delays I saw in the field records.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I feel we are all being so thoughtful. If we prioritize a project that creates a lasting resource, like a catalog, it would be a wonderful gift to the future of the field.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
47,2,4,pass,Shizue,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
48,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree with Shizue. A project that combines a lasting resource with our current staffing strengths and financial subsidies would be the most rational and secure investment.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
49,2,4,pass,Ryuji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. We should seek a candidate that avoids the spectroscopy risks and the animal costs, while leveraging the stable glasshouse crew and the efficient repository.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
51,2,4,pass,Victoria,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a most elegant consensus. We shall seek a candidate that avoids the financial drain of the vivarium and the fragility of the spectroscopy suite, favoring instead the stability of the glasshouse and the digital realm.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
53,2,4,pass,Benjamin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree completely. It feels right to choose a path that protects the researchers from unnecessary stress and ensures the project can actually reach completion. I am looking forward to seeing the candidates!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
